      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/28/milo-yiannopoulos-detained-ice",
      "description": "<p>A former editor of Breitbart News, Yiannopoulos has also served as an intern for Marjorie Taylor Greene</p><p>Milo Yiannopoulos, a far-right British political commentator, was detained by Immigration and Customs Enforcement in Louisiana, according to the Department of Homeland Security (DHS).</p><p>In a statement on Friday, a DHS spokesperson said that Yiannopoulos was arrested on Thursday at the Louis Armstrong New Orleans international airport (MSY). The spokesperson said Yiannopoulos “legally entered the country” in May 2019, but that “he chose to overstay his welcome in violation of our nation’s laws”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/28/milo-yiannopoulos-detained-ice\">Continue reading...</a>",
